    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d160-a1-a1">

                <pb facs="0295" n="253" xml:id="pg253"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to Lord
                        Russell.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-04-11"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 11, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: I have the honor to enclose to your
                    lordship a slip, extracted from the London Times of to-day, touching the case of
                    the vessel now called the Japan, but named at Greenock lately the Virginia. It
                    is needless to add that the statement therein made of the destination of the
                    vessel is known to me to be false. I have reason to believe that she has not
                    gone. The steamer Allar has already transferred to her one 56 gun and four
                    smaller ones, and is expected to return to her.</p>
                <p>I pray your lordship to accept, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Right Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Earl Russell</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
